From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] theme: frost and glass title rows are a frosted band

Owner, 2026-09-18, on libadwaita .50: "titlebars are not frost, they're
light." Frost and glass title rows rendered as a solid light strip. The window
frame painted the frost or glass veil, the window then painted the title-row
band on top of it (0040, @luma_chrome at .92/.88), and the top bar painted
--headerbar-bg-color (.92/.88) on top of both, so three veils stacked to an
opaque slab.

Frost and glass are now one light material with the Shell. The platform's
surface roles are layers sized to composite to the recipe (the frame 62% on
frost and 30% on glass, the title band over it to 76% and 62%), and the top
bar and header bar paint nothing on frost and glass, so the title row is a
frosted band the wallpaper tints through. Title ink is one step deeper than
paper's (#1f262d frost, #161b20 glass) and holds 4.5:1 composited over a black
wallpaper. Glass's dimmed text keeps 88% of the ink, which holds 4.5:1 on a
glass pane over black; frost keeps 0040's 78%.
---
diff --git a/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss b/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
--- a/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
+++ b/src/stylesheet/widgets/_header-bar.scss
@@ -747,3 +747,38 @@
     --dim-opacity: 90%;
   }
 }
+
+// Frost and glass are one light material with the Shell (0041). The title row
+// is not a veil of its own any more: the window's frame is the frosted
+// material, and the title band (@luma_chrome) is a thin layer painted over
+// it, so the title row composites to 76% on frost and 62% on glass -- a
+// frosted band the wallpaper tints through, not a solid white strip. The
+// top bar and the header bar therefore paint nothing themselves; stacking
+// their .92/.88 veils on the frame and the band is what made the title row
+// read as solid. Title ink is one step deeper than paper's so it holds 4.5:1
+// where the band is thinnest, over a black wallpaper.
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost,
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass {
+  --headerbar-bg-color: transparent;
+  --headerbar-backdrop-color: transparent;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-frost {
+  --headerbar-fg-color: #1f262d;
+}
+
+window.csd.luma-treatment-glass {
+  --headerbar-fg-color: #161b20;
+}
+
+// Glass lets the most wallpaper through, so its dimmed text keeps more of the
+// ink: 88% holds 4.5:1 on a glass pane over black, where 78% does not.
+window.luma-treatment-glass {
+  --dim-opacity: 88%;
+}
+
+@media (prefers-contrast: more) {
+  window.luma-treatment-glass {
+    --dim-opacity: 90%;
+  }
+}
